---
import Layout from "../../Base.astro";
import SimpleHero from "../../components/SimpleHero.astro";
import FeaturedArticles from "../../components/FeaturedArticles.astro";
import ServicesRelatedWork from "../../components/ServicesRelatedWork.astro";
import "../../styles/pages/_services-list.scss";
---

<Layout
  title="Digital Design for Websites &amp; Campaigns | Kelp"
  description={`When your digital touchpoints feel disconnected, attention drops and conversions follow. We design digital experiences that are clear, useful, and built around the action you need people to take.`}
>
  <SimpleHero
    tagline="Branding & Design Services"
    title="Digital Design"
    description="When your digital touchpoints feel disconnected, attention drops and conversions follow. We design digital experiences that are clear, useful, and built around the action you need people to take."
    lottieFile="digital-design.json"
  />
  <div class="service-body">
    <div class="wrapper wrapper--narrow">
      <h2>Where teams get stuck</h2>
      <p>
        Businesses often end up with landing pages, emails, product screens, and
        marketing assets that all feel like they came from different places.
        That inconsistency makes the experience harder to trust and harder to
        use.
      </p>
      <p>
        When visitors have to work too hard to understand what they are looking
        at, attention fades before action happens.
      </p>
      <h2>How we fix it</h2>
      <p>
        We design digital experiences with hierarchy, usability, and brand
        consistency in mind so people can quickly understand what matters and
        what to do next.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Web design</li>
        <li>Landing page design</li>
        <li>App design</li>
        <li>Infographic design</li>
        <li>Email design</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Design for Context</h2>
      <p>
        A homepage, product page, paid ad, email, and social post do different
        jobs. We use hierarchy, imagery, motion, and clear calls to action to
        fit each context while keeping the brand recognizable. We also consider
        accessibility, content length, and how the design will adapt when the
        message changes.
      </p>
      <h2>Connect Concept to Production</h2>
      <p>
        Our designers work alongside developers and marketers so a promising
        concept can become a usable page or campaign asset. <a href="/work/elev8-fun/">Elev8 Fun</a> shows
        digital design working with web, paid social, motion, and campaign
        management. Bring us the experience you need to improve.
      </p>
      <h2>How This Works in Practice</h2>
      <p>
        Digital design has to work at the moment someone uses it. A campaign
        asset must lead into a matching landing page; a product graphic must
        clarify a decision; an interface element must remain understandable on a
        small screen. We design the component and its context together, with a
        practical plan for responsive use, accessibility, and future updates by
        the team.
      </p>
      <h2>What the Work Includes</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Website and landing-page interface design</li>
        <li>Campaign and social asset systems</li>
        <li>Responsive layouts and accessibility review</li>
        <li>Developer-ready files and usage guidance</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>What Moving Forward Looks Like</h2>
      <p>
        Show us the channels where the design is failing and the assets your
        team has to produce repeatedly. We can improve a single experience or
        build a broader system for future work.
      </p>
      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <h3>Can Kelp work within our current brand?</h3>
      <p>
        Yes. We can apply existing guidelines, extend them for new digital uses,
        or identify where the system needs refinement.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/contact/" class="button button--green">
          Talk Through Your Design Project
        </a>
      </p>
    </div>
    <ServicesRelatedWork tag={74} />
  </div>
  <FeaturedArticles />
</Layout>
